abstract: "Fully autonomous agentic research. The bound f <= 1 - c/2 on the fully entangled fraction of two-qubit states (Conjecture 2 of Milne, Jennings, Jevtic and Rudolph, arXiv:1404.3951) is prior work, recorded with a claimed Lean proof by the Omega Institute (8 October 2026) and proved in this repository's steering-bounds package; no priority is claimed for it. This package proves the sharp joint bound f <= [sqrt(1+b) + sqrt((1-c)(1-b))]^2/4 in the centre length c and Bob's Bloch length b, classifies all equality cases up to local unitaries, determines the optimal stability constant 4(1+sqrt(1-c))^2, and in every dimension proves a prescribed-Schmidt overlap bound with a complete normal form for its saturators, optimizer-rank bounds, ellipsoid refinements, tensor laws, a qutrit flat-roof counterexample, negativity optimization and collective coupling capacity. Lean proves the frontier, its sharpness, the stability constant, the general overlap bound and the rank ceilings for actual complex matrices. Dev D. Goyal is responsible for publication. No expert validation or peer review is claimed."
